she is elena starkov we can't believe  how dark the new shadow and bone series  could have been had they stuck to the  book  the darkest scene from the novel was  actually tamed down for the series  and the effect it has for our heroine  elena is major  how did the relationship between elena  and kerrigan change from the book to the  show  which characters were made just for the  series  what are you  while the series did make some changes  to what was written in the shadow and  bone novel  including the addition of the characters  from the six of crows book  one of the most surprising changes  definitely came to the end of the season  which was  much darker in the novel when we see  kiergan left behind at the end of season  1 and elena helping bring the skiff and  everyone who'd survived to safety  it makes sense and leaves us feeling  good but the book saw  many more people abandoned instead of  saved the novel had our heroine alina  starkov realizing she could fully  control her powers and fleeing the skiff  with mal  and her protective cone of light into  the shadowfold  yes this means that she left behind not  just kiragan  but everyone who betrayed her and  refused to help her fight  so why did the show make this change  showrunner eric heiser said that with  the inclusion of the characters who  weren't originally in the shadow and  bone book who wound up being on the  skiff in the end  the whole team felt that the connection  and the work the characters of the show  did together  demonstrated teamwork strong enough to  save them the bond was strong and real  so together they could be allies and  support each other  while this does make a major difference  for what we feel about elena  it still does stay in line with the  spirit of the novel and we still see  alina making tough decisions  even if they weren't as grim it wasn't  just that point that was edited though  kiragan's harshness was actually toned  down a bit as well  the book includes a very intense and  harsh speech and a confrontation with  alina  but this was made to be much gentler and  kinder in the show  some of the lines from the conversation  in the book are also instead used in  keurig's conversation with mal  since kiergen is such a complex and  difficult character  something we can definitely all agree on  the team behind the show  felt that whenever a moment of empathy  for kiragan could be added it should be  in order to make him a more accessible  character in the series  as despicable as he is the show  definitely did a great job at making him  a more empathetic character  perhaps even ben barnes who portrayed  him agreed that exploring the humanity  of kierrigan was important  and the actor said he would definitely  be up for continuing that journey into  season two  our fingers are crossed i just want to  talk to you  i've had enough of your lies  speaking of the changes to kiragan's  portrayal there were more  that's right remember that first kiss  alina gives kirigan  well in the books it was kiergen who  made the first move  catching alina off guard when he did it  when things did get a bit steamier  between the two in the novel  they get interrupted but when their  intimate moment comes in the show  kiergen stops and actually makes sure he  has alina's consent  this was added by the actor ben barnes  even while playing a pretty deplorable  character he wanted to make sure the  offer of consent was included with the  addition of the line  we are big fans of these changes and the  creators behind the show had good reason  for it as well  the writers directors and actors of the  show all felt that  since it was based on young adults  novels that there would be a lot of  younger audience members  so it was really important to take the  opportunity to include moments  displaying alina's agency and control  over her choices with her body  as a result the show has sent a really  powerful message about consensual  interactions and portraying a strong  woman with the agency to make the  choices based on what she  actually wants overall the show focuses  on the fantasy of the world  and only includes the more graphic and  risque scenes to serve the storytelling  making it way more about the characters  and the journeys that they go on  the appeal is the story passion and  fantasy  and the team absolutely nails this in  shadow and bone  that means a lot to me  now for the other differences and extras  included in the show that we didn't get  in the novels  of course having the six of crows  characters and zoya as part of the  battle against kiragan was a major  change  later in the trilogy we see zoya and  alina as allies but her inclusion this  early hints that zoya switched sides and  supported elena earlier than the novels  depicted  this pretty much set her up to take on a  major role in a second season which  still falls in line with the progression  of the novels so we're excited to see  where that journey goes  we know that kaz jesper and edge were in  the six of crows novel  but the storylines they have in shadow  and bone were created just for the show  giving us a kind of backstory for all of  them in preparation of what they could  face in the six of crows story  how about mal and elena well mal is a  kinder and more caring person in the  show  always looking out for alina and her  safety what we did miss was the kiss the  two shared in the book  we aren't really sure why it was cut we  did get some suggestive moments of  romance between them  maybe something will happen in season  two while alina's heritage isn't  specified in the book  it was announced before the role was  even cast that elena would be half shoe  giving the opportunity to amplify the  stakes for elena  some lines from the novel were even  adjusted a bit so we could see the  racism that elena  faced as someone who was half shoe in  this world what's a hugh girl doing here  by the way the conductor in general's  latin weren't in the books  they were both characters created just  for the show and they definitely add a  good amount of color and story to the  series  i don't know where it came from came  from everywhere  while the show did take some creative  liberties with shadow and bone and chose  not to go with as dark a story as the  books  it still hits the mark in every way we  definitely hope there's a second season  with a finale like that we need to see  what happens next for elena  how do you feel about the changes the  series made to the story  you
 

